TITLE:: MidinoteCommand
SUMMARY:: Command that sets MIDI note numbers on selected piano-roll notes.
CATEGORIES:: Commands
RELATED:: Classes/Command, Classes/CommandPrompt, Classes/Parameter, Classes/PianoRoll, Classes/PianoRollNote, Classes/SetCommand

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::MidinoteCommand:: is a LINK::Classes/Command:: named CODE::midinote:: that sets the MIDI note number of each selected LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote::. LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: supplies the notes through LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt#-ambientParameters:: as CODE::selectedNotes::.

CODE::values:: is a space-separated list of LINK::Classes/Integer::s from CODE::0:: to CODE::127::. Notes are ordered by CODE::startTime:: only. Notes that share a start time take the same array value; the list wraps and advances only when start time changes. Each note is moved with LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote#-transpose:: by the difference between the target and its current note number, which slides the note view by that many rows. A note that does not respond to CODE::noteNumber:: and CODE::transpose::, such as a LINK::Classes/DrumStep::, is left unchanged.

LINK::#-beforeImage:: records the previous note number of each note whose number will change. LINK::#-restore:: moves those notes back with CODE::transpose::, and moves them forward again from LINK::#-afterImage:: on redo. A note that is already on the target number is left out of the before-image, so an edit that changes nothing is not an undo step.

Example: four notes numbered CODE::60:: at beats CODE::0, 1, 1, 2:: with CODE::midinote values 60 72:: become note numbers CODE::60, 72, 72, 60::.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a new TELETYPE::MidinoteCommand::. Takes no arguments; note numbers are applied by LINK::#-execute::.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::MidinoteCommand:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: afterImage
The note number now stored on each selected note that responds to CODE::noteNumber:: and CODE::transpose::, after LINK::#-execute::.

ARGUMENT:: args
The same arguments dictionary passed to LINK::#-execute::.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/IdentityDictionary:: from note to an event with CODE::\noteNumber::, or CODE::nil:: when no such note was selected.

METHOD:: beforeImage
The note number stored on each selected note whose number differs from the value LINK::#-execute:: would write.

ARGUMENT:: args
The same arguments dictionary about to be passed to LINK::#-execute::.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/IdentityDictionary:: from note to an event with CODE::\noteNumber::, or CODE::nil:: when every selected note is already on its target number.

METHOD:: execute
Applies wrapped MIDI note numbers to CODE::\selectedNotes:: grouped by start time.

ARGUMENT:: args
A LINK::Classes/Dictionary:: or LINK::Classes/Event:: with CODE::\selectedNotes:: (an LINK::Classes/Array:: of notes that respond to CODE::noteNumber:: and CODE::transpose::) and CODE::\values:: (a non-empty LINK::Classes/Array:: of LINK::Classes/Integer::s from CODE::0:: to CODE::127::).

METHOD:: restore
Moves each note to the CODE::\noteNumber:: stored in an image from LINK::#-beforeImage:: or LINK::#-afterImage::, using CODE::transpose:: so the note view slides with it.

ARGUMENT:: image
An LINK::Classes/IdentityDictionary:: from note to an event with CODE::\noteNumber::, or CODE::nil::.

PRIVATE:: prEachTarget
